## Original Content
A China-donated smart rehabilitation device was officially handed over and put into use at the Clinical Emergency Hospital in Bishkek, capital of Kyrgyzstan on August 22, 2026.

## Summary
A smart rehabilitation device donated by China has been officially handed over and put into use at the Clinical Emergency Hospital in Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan, on August 22, 2026. This event highlights a healthcare collaboration between China and Kyrgyzstan through the deployment of advanced medical technology.

## Key Points
- China donated a smart rehabilitation device to support healthcare in Kyrgyzstan.
- The device is now operational at the Clinical Emergency Hospital in Bishkek, enhancing local medical capabilities.
- The handover and implementation occurred on August 22, 2026, marking a milestone in international healthcare aid.


